    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 telephone for humans while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the other derived read-only fields like `membershipNumber`, `locality`, etc.), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and serializes it in `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived `getTelephoneDisplay()` getter (plus a small `extractCountryCode` helper). It:\n- Returns the stored value unchanged if it isn't a `+`-prefixed digit string.\n- Splits off the country code (preferring the known fixed-length codes `+61` \u2192 9 national digits and `+1` \u2192 10, falling back to the leading digit), keeps it after the `+`, then groups the national digits in threes from the left separated by spaces.\n- Example: stored `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\nMapStruct auto-maps the new getter onto the DTO by name (same mechanism as the existing derived getters), so no mapper or controller changes were needed. The raw `telephone` continues to be stored and returned in E.164 form (`+61412345678`), exactly as the test asserts.",
